  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 556ecd75ee852ce4a93c60357c4eb4f6, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Cara amica,


    Giulia once more. My cousin from Genoa heard I was
    writing to you and insisted I send this one. She says I make pesto "like a Roman,"
    which is not a compliment.


    Basil, a little cheese, good oil, crushed together
    until it turns bright green. Never cook the pesto. Toss it with the hot pasta
    and let the warmth do the work.


    My cousin and I still argue about it every
    summer. We also eat it together every summer.


    Family is the people you
    argue with and still share a table with.'
